--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -1 +1 @@
-- `hse query-pack` — the manual operator query pack. For a target it generates the ranked queries to run BY HAND against the manual/paid exposure providers HSE cannot auto-query without an entitlement (IntelX, OathNet, Stolen.tax, DeHashed, XposedOrNot, HIBP), each with its query type, the provider surface to run it on, the expected result class (a multi-source gateway is flagged as non-independent; a HIBP miss is flagged as not proof of absence), and a stable `parent_query_id` grouping the pack under one seed. Purely offline and deterministic — it emits queries and destinations, makes no network call, and so declares no provider API contract. Scope is discovery / exposure verification / correlation only; it never emits account-takeover, credential-stuffing, session-replay, or authentication-bypass workflows. Every provider surface is a domain the codebase already reaches through that provider's module, so it points only at services HSE has itself verified.
+- `hse query-pack` — the manual operator query pack. For a target it generates the ranked queries to run BY HAND against ten verified exposure-provider surfaces (IntelX, Hudson Rock, OathNet, NiamonX, SeekNow, Stolen.tax, DeHashed, LeakCheck, XposedOrNot, HIBP) for entitlement-gated lookup or manual cross-checking, each with its query type, the provider surface to run it on, the expected result class (a multi-source gateway is flagged as non-independent; a HIBP miss is flagged as not proof of absence), and a stable `parent_query_id` grouping the pack under one seed. Purely offline and deterministic — it emits queries and destinations, makes no network call, and so declares no provider API contract. Scope is discovery / exposure verification / correlation only; it never emits account-takeover, credential-stuffing, session-replay, or authentication-bypass workflows. Every provider surface is a domain the codebase already reaches through that provider's module, so it points only at services HSE has itself verified.
